      "title": "Polygon (MATIC)",
      "section": "What it is",
      "score": 0.741,
      "text": "## What it is\n\nPolygon is a suite of scaling solutions for Ethereum. The flagship is\nPolygon PoS, a sidechain compatible with the Ethereum Virtual Machine\nthat processes transactions cheaply and quickly while periodically\ncheckpointing to Ethereum. The broader Polygon stack now includes zkEVM,\nPolygon CDK, and the AggLayer for cross-chain coordination."
    },
    {
      "title": "Polygon (MATIC)",
      "section": "Why it exists",
      "score": 0.734,
      "text": "## Why it exists\n\nIn Ethereum's high-fee periods, ordinary transactions could cost tens\nof dollars. Polygon was designed to give Ethereum users a near-identical\ndeveloper experience at a tiny fraction of the cost, capturing\napplications that needed Ethereum's security profile without its\nmainnet fees."
    },
    {
      "title": "Polygon (MATIC)",
      "section": "Notable context",
      "score": 0.727,
      "text": "## Notable context\n\nPolygon was an early winner of the layer-2 narrative, hosting major\napplications like Aave, Uniswap, and OpenSea Polygon markets. The\nproject announced Polygon 2.0 in 2023, including a token migration from\nMATIC to POL and a more unified architecture. MATIC reached its peak\nnear $2.90 in December 2021 before retreating with the broader market."
    },
    {
      "title": "Polygon (MATIC)",
      "section": "Key facts",
      "score": 0.716,
      "text": "## Key facts\n\n- **Type**: Ethereum scaling ecosystem (sidechain + ZK rollup + SDK)\n- **Native token**: MATIC (transitioning to POL under Polygon 2.0)\n- **Supply**: Capped at 10 billion MATIC\n- **Founders**: Jaynti Kanani, Sandeep Nailwal, Anurag Arjun (and others)\n- **Mainnet launch**: May 2020 (as Matic Network); rebranded to Polygon\n  in February 2021"
    }
  ]
}

